 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Compact metrizable spaces are second countable",
 "statement": "Use the universes of [def-weil-size-convention]. Let $X$ be a compact metrizable topological space. Then $X$ is second countable: there exists a countable family $\\mathcal B$ of open subsets of $X$ such that every open subset of $X$ is a union of members of $\\mathcal B$.",
 "source": {
